{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35877-wraith20-and-post-5gm","id":35877,"title":"Wraith20 and post-5GM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T16:06:45-08:00","id":35877,"title":"Wraith20 and post-5GM","content":"Should Wraith20 address the World of Darkness as it existed after the coming of the Fifth Great Maelstrom? And if so, how? <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b> spoke of ghosts being forced across the Shroud and latching onto corpses and other anchors that they had no business being attached to, which opens up interesting possibilities for the Risen; and <b>Orpheus</b> picks up five years later, with the premise that all of the pre-5GM ghosts got wiped out \u2014 which leads to a very different kind of setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T16:28:14-08:00","id":35899,"title":"","content":"You mean the Sixth Great Maelstrom. The Fifth was World War 2 and the Holocaust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T16:34:14-08:00","id":35905,"title":"","content":"I don't think it should. V20 isn't post-Gehenna. W20 isn't post-Apocalypse. Why would Wr20 be post-Maelstrom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T18:22:43-08:00","id":35974,"title":"","content":"The whatever-20 books are metaplot agnostic, and the new Void Engineers book basically said &quot;this is a timeline in which 2005 came and went with no great end of the world.&quot; I like that stance and don't see it changing for Wr20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T19:02:34-08:00","id":36002,"title":"","content":"Given the tone of V20 and W20, I'd say the obvious option is for Wr20 to be set on the cusp of the 6th Great Maelstrom/the End of Empire story-line.<br /> <br /> Having some material for the 6th going off and what the Underworld looks like afterwards (considering that the 6th does not represent the same level of setting-ending-level doom that Gehenna does) seems likely though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T20:24:45-08:00","id":36051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35877-wraith20-and-post-5gm?p=36002#post36002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the tone of V20 and W20, I'd say the obvious option is for Wr20 to be set on the cusp of the 6th Great Maelstrom/the End of Empire story-line.<br /> <br /> Having some material for the 6th going off and what the Underworld looks like afterwards (considering that the 6th does not represent the same level of setting-ending-level doom that Gehenna does) seems likely though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't the 6th wreck the Underworld so thoroughly that it was entirely restructured, resulting in the Stormwall sealing off the old underworld entirely? Or was that helped along by something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:28:55-08:00","id":36089,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the 20th books work on a postponed system.<br /> Essentially, the idea that things are ending still exists as much as you want it.<br /> You can have the Gehenna or 6th Maelstrom imminently, but you could just as easily not have it, or have it a bit down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:42:10-08:00","id":36157,"title":"","content":"One difference is that the 6GM occurred in the WoD at a point that changed the metaphysics of the overall setting and ushered in several new gamelines. If I want to run V20 before or after the Week of Nightmares, I can; if I want to run M20 after the coming of the Avatar Storm, I can. If I want to do a crossover between Vampire and Mage that takes place in the wake of said disasters (which coincided), I can. <br /> <br /> End of Empire differs from the other \u201cLast Books\u201d of the oWoD in that it came early and impacted other gamelines. There were no Imbued before te Ghost-Storm; nor were there any Amenti or Fallen (there were mummies; but they were drastically different).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T06:28:24-08:00","id":36338,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Though that isn't stopping the X20 line from referencing them even though they shouldn't exist in the default setting.<br /> <br /> And this is also why I want there to be a Wr20 book that deals with a post-6GM world. Honestly too much there to be squeezed into the Wr20 Rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T16:29:14-08:00","id":37060,"title":"","content":"I'd personally like to see Wraith20 be Orpheus-friendly myself. Unless Orpheus is being wrapped into Wraith as a Setting Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T19:12:20-08:00","id":37602,"title":"","content":"Why does this keep getting brought up? Richard Dansky himself keeps pointing out NO Orpheus. Wraith 20 is going to be about Wraith. It's going to be set before tge last great Maelstrom and the logistics for conflicting content will be something he'll have to work out. Go read the Ask the Deadguy thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T20:28:05-08:00","id":37650,"title":"","content":"I have: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34987-ask-the-deadguy?p=36017#post36017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-I love me some Orpheus. Lucien Soulban and I go way, way back, and I really enjoy his work. It was a pleasure and an honor to contribute to the first Orpheus book, and I think there's a lot that's really great in the game. I'm certainly not going to ignore it when it comes time to have the rubber hit the road on Wraith 20; that being said, the focus of Wraith is going to be - big shock reveal here - Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cI\u2019m certainly not going to ignore it\u201d does not sound to me like \u201cNO Orpheus\u201d. As for when it will be set, the 20th Anniversary Editions have traditionally been setting-agnostic, and Richard has commented that he\u2019s debating how to handle Grandmother, an entity that wasn\u2019t introduced until the last books of Orpheus \u2014 so it\u2019s sounding like Wraith20 <i>will</i> support post-6GM games \u2014 though I don\u2019t expect that to be the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T21:10:39-08:00","id":37668,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Given that Orpheus was the spiritual successor to WtO it would be hard to completely ignore it. Which is another thing that sets Orpheus apart from the other late era CWoD lines. In many ways Orpheus is a continuation of Wraith. While not everything in the two gamelines mesh together perfectly what they in common is greater than what they don't.<br /> <br /> And I've often wondered if some of the Orpheus concepts like Grandmother and the Orphan-Grinders were unused WtO ideas or inspired by unused ideas.<br /> <br /> Another thing that sets Orpheus apart from the other late era lines is that its existence is not dependent on the 6GM*. While the Orpheus Group was created for the gameline within the universe Orpheus not existed before the 6GM but were already deeply involved in projection experiments and investigations into the world of ghosts.<br /> <br /> *Yes there were Fallen that had escaped their prison one way or another but their numbers were not on the level they were after it, the numbers that really made them what they are in DtF.<br /> <br /> Now as I've said before elsewhere I don't expect the Wr20 Rulebook to talk much about Orpheus but I would like a mention of it within the book, which I feel it deserves even if it's just a couple sentences within a section talking about groups from the Skinlands that investigate ghosts. And I would really love a later book that bridges Wraith with Orpheus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T21:22:54-08:00","id":37675,"title":"","content":"As I\u2019ve mentioned before, my own preference would be to mention Orpheus in whatever section describes the various ghost-hunter factions, and described as an up-and-coming player that is just starting to delve into matters of the afterlife. Then include a hint of what\u2019s in store for the company, paired with a reference to the Orpheus series on DTRPG for those who are interested in more details about them. If there\u2019s sufficient interest (STRETCH GOAL!), consider something like a Translation Guide involving Wraith and Orpheus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T22:28:37-08:00","id":37711,"title":"","content":"I'd kill to see a Translation Guide as a Stretch Goal.<br /> <br /> Related to the subject at hand; could a Wraith-era Spectre become an Orphan-Grinder? There's mention somewhere Spectre PCs are discussed (either The Great War or Dark Reflections) of Mutiles/Mortwrights seeking out redemption, and the Psyche harasses them the same way the Shadow harasses normal Wraiths. I know there's minor cosmology differences, but I don't see any reason for it to not be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T23:23:08-08:00","id":37728,"title":"","content":"&quot;The focus of Wraith 20 is going to be - big shock reveal here - Wraith&quot; seems like a pretty conclusive statement. Orpheus may touch on the Wraith universe, but as it keeps getting pointed out, it's not Wraith. While I agree that Orpheus would be a great continuation of Wraith it comes after the last Maelstrom which, if Wr20 follows the pattern of the other XX editions, will be set in an ambiguous time before such events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T00:14:21-08:00","id":37742,"title":"","content":"The 20th books have been 550 page tomes. Even if you can't run Orpheus out of Wr20's core book, it seems pretty clear that Rich is considering incorporating Orpheus into the Wr20 line in some fashion. He's said he's not ignoring it and he's not focusing on it. That's tends to indicate the path between pre-6th GM and post, including Orpheus, is going to be accounted for; and possibly better integrated into how things got from one side of the event to the other. Whether that means Orpheus &quot;20th&quot; ends up part of Wr20's line of books or it eventually gets its own compilation later is the only real question. Considering Orpheus' rather short run, it seems to make more sense to have it be a supplement to Wr20 than something independent. And a more unified system between the two would make games that transition through the 6th GM that'll be looming on the horizon of Wr20 likely default that much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T01:50:17-08:00","id":37762,"title":"","content":"Darling_Rose: you\u2019re selectively reading Richard\u2019s post. \u201cI won\u2019t focus on Orpheus\u201d doesn\u2019t mean \u201cI won\u2019t say anything about Orpheus\u201d; and \u201cI won\u2019t ignore Orpheus\u201d pretty much <i>does</i> mean \u201cI\u2019ll talk about Orpheus somewhere, in some capacity\u201d. It just won\u2019t be the focus of the game \u2014 nor would I expect it to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-27-2013, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T05:46:44-08:00","id":37805,"title":"","content":"Indeed and that's what we've all been saying. None of us expect them to put a lot of Orpheus in Wr20 but given how interconnected they are it makes sense to include a mention of them, that's what we want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T21:18:11-08:00","id":38574,"title":"","content":"I was surprised they went with giving the Wraith the v20 treatment, but as a fan, I was very happy to hear about it. As the others mentioned, it will probably be the aftermath of Ends of the Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T21:59:36-08:00","id":38590,"title":"","content":"Not likely. Wr20 will be pre-6GM for a couple reasons. 1) The X20th Anniversary Editions are well like their name implies Anniversary books, they aren't really meant to push the metaplot forward but to serve as a celebration of the game and comprehensive collection of everything you'd need to really play the game. 2) The default setting of all the X20 books is the 2nd Edition time period, before the 6GM happened and ushered in the beginning of the Time of Judgement. 3) They'd have to, at the very least, remake the setting of Wraith if it was set post-6GM just because of what the storm wrought in the Underworld. And again that's not the X20 Edition's purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T22:34:16-08:00","id":38601,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Regarding the Sixth Great Maelstrom and\u2026&lt;wait for it&gt;\u2026 the Meta-plot:<br /> <br /> Unlike the TOJ scenarios, Wraith had ONE (official ending) to the Storyline. From that storyline, we get the Sixth Great Maelstrom, some other nasty stuff, cracks forming in the Abyss, and Demons running around (as per Demon the Fallen). Here\u2019s the thing; in a Wraith game, I don\u2019t think that matters. [IIRC, didn\u2019t some Demon book try to make Charon a Slayer? My absent Emperor, an emo-angel? No.]<br /> <br /> My opinion on the meta-plot and the Sixth Great Maelstrom: Leave it out. At least as the Wr20 default setting. Maybe a small sub-chapter that details some<i> guidelines </i>for running games in this ruined and storm-riddled Underworld, but the idea of the Underworld \u201cstill spinning\u201d is appealing. <br /> <br /> Don\u2019t get me wrong. If that\u2019s something that your troupe wants to run, that\u2019s cool and there\u2019s nothing wrong with that. I would have loved run it with my troupe. <i>Ends of Empire</i> is still available via Drivethrurpg.com and I think having your players and characters as the stars of the <i>Chuck Anderson Reunion Show </i>is more fitting then defaulting to some new and random Deathlords. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T22:38:42-08:00","id":38602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35877-wraith20-and-post-5gm?p=38601#post38601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Regarding the Sixth Great Maelstrom and\u2026&lt;wait for it&gt;\u2026 the Meta-plot:<br /> <br /> Unlike the TOJ scenarios, Wraith had ONE (official ending) to the Storyline. From that storyline, we get the Sixth Great Maelstrom, some other nasty stuff, cracks forming in the Abyss, and Demons running around (as per Demon the Fallen). Here\u2019s the thing; in a Wraith game, I don\u2019t think that matters. [IIRC, didn\u2019t some Demon book try to make Charon a Slayer? My absent Emperor, an emo-angel? No.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Charon the Emperor took Charon the demon's name (the point of connection being the Lady of Fate, who knew them both).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T22:43:51-08:00","id":38604,"title":"","content":"My hope is that Wraith20 will be set primarily before the 6GM, but will include support for gaming after it as well: e.g., rules for what the Underworld is like with the Ghost-Storm in full force, rules for post-Reckoning Risen, etc. Again, not as the default; but maybe as an Appendix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T22:49:20-08:00","id":38606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35877-wraith20-and-post-5gm?p=38602#post38602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charon the Emperor took Charon the demon's name (the point of connection being the Lady of Fate, who knew them both).</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Wraith book or Demon book?<br /> If Wraith, I'm ignoring it.<br /> If Demon, I don't care.<br /> <br /> So, I guess it doesn't matter what book it's from. I love it when I answer my own questions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","user":"Nazfool","date":". 12-29-2013, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T22:53:04-08:00","id":38607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35877-wraith20-and-post-5gm?p=38604#post38604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My hope is that Wraith20 will be set primarily before the 6GM, but will include support for gaming after it as well: e.g., rules for what the Underworld is like with the Ghost-Storm in full force, rules for post-Reckoning Risen, etc. Again, not as the default; but maybe as an Appendix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. You summed up my opinion nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}